<mxCell id="fnote" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="FK partner_id / customer_partner_id (customer_sales_profiles, customer_credit_profiles, sales_portal_tokens, opp_hdrs, quot_hdrs, so_hdrs, ret_hdrs) references CRM.partners.id — cross-schema, Core-peer read, no local edge drawn (Sales never writes into CRM, never models a second Customer table). owner_id/rep_id/user_id-style references point to Laravel&#39;s own users table, outside this schema — no edge drawn. so_hdrs/quot_hdrs/ret_hdrs.subject_type+subject_id are deliberately plain informational columns (e.g. &#39;legal.matters&#39;), not a foreign key — no edge drawn, per the one-way Core-has-zero-knowledge-of-Vertical rule (§5). Invoices, invoice lines, and payments are NOT modeled here by design: Sales fires InvoiceRequested/PaymentRequested into ACCOUNTING.ar_invoices/ar_payments, which is the single AR ledger of record (§3I/§5) — so_lines.qty_invoiced is only a rollup counter, updated when Accounting echoes back InvoicePosted/PaymentRecorded. inventory_goods_issue_id (dlv_hdrs) is an informational reference to INVENTORY.goods_issues.id, not an enforced FK, since Inventory is an optional install (§3H/§5) — no edge drawn." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1468" width="1750" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
